request.user_message:
Abstract the following semantic predicate cluster into exactly one reusable predicate.

Cluster ID:
unary-013

Cluster Arity:
1

Cluster Members:
[
  {
    "name": "JUSTIFIES_NUMERICAL_EQUIVALENCE_BY_ERROR_ANALYSIS",
    "definition": "The reasoning derives or bounds the magnitude of accumulated numerical error expected from a proposed computation and compares that magnitude with the required equivalence tolerance, concluding that the produced results will or will not be accepted as equivalent.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The agent text performing the error-magnitude derivation or bound and the comparison against the required tolerance."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning quantifies an expected error magnitude or worst-case bound for the proposed computation, for example from the number of accumulation steps and machine epsilon.",
      "The reasoning explicitly relates that magnitude to the stated tolerance and concludes that the tolerance will or will not be met."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning asserts correctness or equivalence without deriving or bounding any error magnitude.",
      "The quantified quantity concerns something other than numerical accuracy, such as runtime, memory, or cost.",
      "The error magnitude is only taken from an already reported measurement rather than derived or estimated for the proposed computation."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "PREDICTS_PERFORMANCE_FROM_COMPLEXITY_ESTIMATE",
    "definition": "The reasoning estimates the time or resource cost of one or more implementations, operations, or commands from operation counts, data sizes, conversion overhead, or algorithmic complexity, and uses that estimate to judge whether a performance requirement will be met or to choose how a command should be executed.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The agent text containing the cost, operation-count, or duration estimate and the judgement or execution decision drawn from it."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning gives a quantitative cost, operation-count, or duration estimate for at least one implementation, operation, or command, before the corresponding outcome is observed.",
      "The estimate is used either to conclude that a performance requirement will be met or violated, or to decide how a command should be executed, such as its expected duration, timeout, or background execution."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning names a performance requirement without estimating any cost or duration.",
      "The estimate concerns numerical accuracy or correctness rather than time or resource cost.",
      "The estimate is stated but no performance judgement or execution decision is drawn from it."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "IDENTIFIES_PERFORMANCE_BOTTLENECK",
    "definition": "The reasoning localizes the dominant share of a measured runtime to a specific stage, component, or operation in the execution pipeline, using timing evidence, and presents that localization as the reason to optimize or redesign that stage.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The agent text attributing most of the measured runtime to a specific stage or component and motivating optimization of it."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning references a measured runtime, timing breakdown, or comparable quantitative performance evidence.",
      "The reasoning attributes the dominant cost to an identifiable stage, component, or operation rather than to the system as a whole.",
      "The reasoning presents the identified bottleneck as the reason to redesign or optimize that stage."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning states only that performance is inadequate without locating a dominant cost.",
      "The reasoning proposes optimizations unrelated to any identified cost contributor.",
      "The timing evidence is used only to check a threshold, with no stage or component singled out as the dominant cost."
    ]
  }
]

Previously Generated Predicate Names:
["CONFIGURES_EVENT_DRIVEN_AUTOMATION", "PREVENTS_SELF_CAUSED_ADVERSE_EFFECTS_THROUGH_CORRECTIVE_ACTION", "EVALUATES_CANDIDATE_AGAINST_ENUMERATED_CONSTRAINTS_OR_SCENARIOS", "RESOLVES_EVALUATED_CANDIDATE_ELEMENTS_TO_SINGLE_RESULT", "INTERPRETS_REQUIREMENTS_FOR_ACTION_ADMISSIBILITY", "INITIATES_DETACHED_ASYNCHRONOUS_EXECUTION", "REPORTS_ABSENT_OR_UNAVAILABLE_CAPABILITY", "IDENTIFIES_SPECIFIC_POTENTIAL_FAILURE_MODE", "ASSESSES_COMPETING_ACCOUNTS_OF_SAME_OBSERVATION", "ESTABLISHES_EVIDENCE_GROUNDED_TASK_OUTCOME_REFERENCE", "FORMULATES_STRUCTURED_OPERATIVE_ACCOUNT", "SPECIFIES_TARGET_LINKED_CONCRETE_MEANS"]

Read every member's complete definition, ordered parameters, assertion conditions, and exclusion conditions. Identify the common underlying behavioral mechanism and generate exactly one complete predicate following the system instructions. The new predicate must preserve the cluster arity. Use a unique predicate name that does not conflict with previously generated predicate names. Return only the complete five-field JSON predicate.

message.content:
{
  "name": "GROUNDS_COMPUTATIONAL_ASSESSMENT_IN_QUANTITATIVE_ANALYSIS",
  "definition": "The reasoning performs a quantitative analysis of a computational process—deriving or bounding numerical error, estimating time or resource cost from operation counts or data sizes, or using timing evidence to attribute dominant cost—and uses the quantified result to judge whether a stated numerical or performance requirement will be met, to decide how a computation should be executed, or to identify the stage or component that should be optimized.",
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "quantitative_reasoning",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "description": "The agent text containing the quantitative estimate, error bound, cost calculation, timing breakdown, or dominant-cost attribution together with the judgment, execution decision, or optimization target derived from it."
    }
  ],
  "assertion_conditions": [
    "The reasoning supplies a quantitative estimate, bound, measured timing breakdown, or cost attribution for a computational process or component.",
    "The reasoning explicitly relates the quantified result to a stated numerical tolerance or performance requirement, or uses it to decide execution strategy or to single out a dominant cost contributor for optimization.",
    "The reasoning derives a conclusion or recommendation—such as equivalence acceptance, performance satisfaction or violation, execution choice, or optimization target—from that quantified result rather than from qualitative assertion alone."
  ],
  "exclusion_conditions": [
    "The reasoning asserts correctness, equivalence, performance adequacy, or need for optimization without any quantitative estimate, bound, timing measurement, or cost attribution.",
    "The quantified quantity does not concern numerical accuracy, time, resource cost, or execution-cost attribution, but some unrelated property such as monetary price or probability.",
    "A quantitative estimate or timing measurement is mentioned but neither compared with a requirement nor used to make an execution decision or localize a dominant cost; it is only incidental information.",
    "The error magnitude or performance number is merely reported as a final observed outcome with no derivation, bounding, estimation, comparison, or attribution to a computational component."
  ]
}

